  "originalQuery": "As a Database Engineer, you are responsible for periodically testing the disaster recovery strategy of a large-scale, multi-tier application. The goal is to ensure the effectiveness of the disaster recovery plan while minimizing the impact on production workloads. Which of the following options is the most suitable approach for testing the disaster recovery plan while maintaining production performance and ensuring accurate test results?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Create a separate environment mirroring the production environment and use real-time database replication to conduct disaster recovery tests.<br/>B. Use a scheduled maintenance window to conduct disaster recovery tests on the production environment.<br/>C. Introduce random faults into the production environment to test the system's resilience.<br/>D. Implement a canary deployment strategy, where a small portion of the production environment is used for testing disaster recovery scenarios.",
